<title>SINGAPORE: Two Chinese crude units restarted in end-April.</title>
<headline>Two Chinese crude units restarted in end-April.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Chinese refineries in Dalian and Guangzhou have resumed operations in end April following scheduled maintenance turnarounds, refinery sources said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The 100,000-barrel-per-day (bpd) Dalian West Pacific Petroleum Company (WEPEC) has completed maintenance works late last month and operations have resumed, a source at the refinery said.</p>
<p>WEPEC is jointly owned by several Chinese refineries and French oil company Total.</p>
<p>China's 120-140,000-bpd Guangzhou refinery has also restarted in end April following scheduled maintenance turnaround, a company source in Guangzhou said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65 870 3571)</p>
